        "event": "Heat Advisory",
        "headline": "Heat Advisory issued August 9 at 11:56AM AKDT until August 10 at 8:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Very warm afternoon temperatures in the middle to upper\n70s, with overnight temperatures in the low to mid 50s.\n\n* WHERE...Lower Matanuska Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM AKDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Individuals not accustomed to these unusually warm\ntemperatures for this region may experience heat related illnesses.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-08-09T11:56:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-08-10T06:15:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Lower Matanuska Valley",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids and check up on elderly and vulnerable\nrelatives and neighbors.\n\nTake extra precautions when working in the sun. Wear sunscreen and\nlightweight, loose fitting clothing. Try to limit strenuous\nactivities to early morning or evening. Take action when you see\nsymptoms of heat exh",
